<%# For lists too long to send to the page. Opening it asks the url for a
    starting list, and typing asks again with ?q=. In a slow search the
    magnifying glass turns into a spinner. The docs site answers /demo/customers;
    point url: at your own endpoint, which can look like this:

      # config/routes.rb
      get "customers/search", to: "customers#search"

      # app/controllers/customers_controller.rb
      def search
        query = Customer.sanitize_sql_like(params[:q].to_s)
        customers = Customer.where("name ILIKE ?", "%#{query}%").order(:name).limit(20)
        render json: customers.map { |customer| { value: customer.id, label: customer.name } }
      end

    On an edit form, pass the current choice as options:, so it's named before
    anything is fetched. %>
<div class="grid max-w-xl gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
  <%= render(UI::Select.new(name: "customer_id", url: "/demo/customers", label: "Customer", prompt: "Find a customer")) %>
  <%= render(UI::Select.new(name: "customer_ids", url: "/demo/customers", label: "Copy invoices to", multiple: true,
                            options: [ [ "Aditi Rao Traders", 2001 ] ], selected: [ 2001 ])) %>
</div>
